{"entryId":"3212","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3212:1","sourceSha256":"b9536d6c2050ebf1b6bfc5d80031b3c92407dd28fd44a133238943d9c2301841","englishSha256":"69323afd45fbda492b0025ccbc2701ff9de54be6f3aa93a3c18c3d9e02ef36d2","citations":[{"id":"3212:1:link-001","he":[13,74],"en":[56,87],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_Mitzvot_Gadol%2C_Negative_Commandments_193.1"},"reference":"Sefer Mitzvot Gadol, Negative Commandments 193:1","assessment":"Semag negative commandment 193 explicitly connects the Rav Yosef exchange in Hullin with the earlier Ravina of the mortgage case. The physical foliation belongs to Heilprin’s cited edition.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Mitzvot Gadol, Negative Commandments 193:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_Mitzvot_Gadol%2C_Negative_Commandments_193.1"},"witness":"Munkatch, 1901"},{"reference":"Chullin 48a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_48a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-002","he":[75,117],"en":[131,150],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin_48a.8.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Chullin 48a:8:1","assessment":"The Tosafot passage says “perhaps” this is a different Ravina; Rosh independently gives the earlier-person explanation. Preserve the different formulations.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Chullin 48a:8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin_48a.8.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-003","he":[75,117],"en":[156,176],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","assessment":"The Tosafot passage says “perhaps” this is a different Ravina; Rosh independently gives the earlier-person explanation. Preserve the different formulations.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Chullin 48a:8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin_48a.8.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-004","he":[118,221],"en":[184,369],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_48a.8"},"reference":"Chullin 48a:8","assessment":"Hullin gives the direct response by Rav Yosef, while Kiddushin states the literary succession tradition. The chronological distinction is the medieval sources’ inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 48a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_48a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-005","he":[223,310],"en":[395,412],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.21"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:21","assessment":"Rosh quotes the two speakers in this order. It is likewise the order of the checked folio. Order is a datum; age is an inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:22","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.22"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-006","he":[311,366],"en":[483,573],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","assessment":"The Rosh continues in those terms. Kiddushin supports the first clause as a succession tradition; it does not contain the pupil-colleague assertion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-007","he":[368,409],"en":[620,631],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Sanhedrin_9.2.1"},"reference":"Rosh on Sanhedrin 9:2:1","assessment":"Rosh makes the earlier-namesakes argument in the opening chapter’s confinement case, and the earlier Heilprin dossier explicitly cites it.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rosh on Sanhedrin 9:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Sanhedrin_9.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 77a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_77a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 291:1","target":{"entry":291,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-008","he":[368,409],"en":[644,659],"target":{"entry":291,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 291:1","assessment":"Rosh makes the earlier-namesakes argument in the opening chapter’s confinement case, and the earlier Heilprin dossier explicitly cites it.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 291:1","target":{"entry":291,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Rosh on Sanhedrin 9:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Sanhedrin_9.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 77a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_77a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-009","he":[410,439],"en":[662,671],"target":{"entry":3215,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 3215:1","assessment":"The later Ravina dossier cites the Be’er Sheva argument. The source independently lists the Ravina/Rava passages and the Rav Ashi succession objection.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3215:1","target":{"entry":3215,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Be'er Sheva 11:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Be%27er_Sheva_11.4"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1890"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-010","he":[410,439],"en":[694,705],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Be%27er_Sheva_11.4"},"reference":"Be'er Sheva 11:4","assessment":"The later Ravina dossier cites the Be’er Sheva argument. The source independently lists the Ravina/Rava passages and the Rav Ashi succession objection.","evidence":[{"reference":"Be'er Sheva 11:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Be%27er_Sheva_11.4"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1890"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3215:1","target":{"entry":3215,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-011","he":[441,488],"en":[730,762],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","assessment":"The checked Shittah text reads תלמיד הר״ף, normally read as a pupil of Rabbenu Peretz, where Heilprin’s text has הריא״ף. Its later chronological argument appears after a separate “and in the Shittah it is written” heading in the checked passage.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-012","he":[489,632],"en":[993,1021],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_62a.15"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 62a:15","assessment":"The received Shittah directly gives the question and the two-Ravinas solution as one explanation. Bava Metzia 62a is the comparison passage with Rav Ashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 62a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_62a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-013","he":[633,712],"en":[1149,1290],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","assessment":"This passage spans the end of the cited pupil’s comparison and the separate anonymous Shittah argument. The Hullin wording is exact.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"},{"reference":"Chullin 48a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_48a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-014","he":[785,824],"en":[1375,1438],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_49a.4"},"reference":"Chullin 49a:4","assessment":"The formula is attested verbatim in Hullin, and the checked Shittah quotes it as part of the separate chronological argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 49a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_49a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 53b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_53b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-015","he":[885,963],"en":[1544,1656],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.21"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:21","assessment":"The statement order directly matches both Bavli and Shittah. The chronological application belongs to the commentator.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 28a:22","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_28a.22"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-016","he":[970,1076],"en":[1689,1728],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.9"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:9","assessment":"The checked primary text confirms Rabbah and Rav Pappi. The latter differs from Rav Pappa in the received Shittah chronology argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-017","he":[970,1076],"en":[1737,1791],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","assessment":"The checked primary text confirms Rabbah and Rav Pappi. The latter differs from Rav Pappa in the received Shittah chronology argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-018","he":[1078,1123],"en":[1839,1921],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_82a.5"},"reference":"Chullin 82a:5","assessment":"Hullin 82a supplies the exact formula in the named chapter. Hullin 77a independently also gives the formula with Rav Pappi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 82a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_82a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 77a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_77a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-019","he":[1175,1305],"en":[2021,2029],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.6"},"reference":"Yoma 78a:6","assessment":"The Bavli places Rav Rehumi’s report in the preceding passage. Tosafot Yeshanim use it as an objection and offer two possibilities: distinct Ravinas, or an answer Ravina did not himself accept. Rav Rehumi’s observation is not part of Ravina’s direct speech.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 78a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 78a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_78a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Yoma 78a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-020","he":[1175,1305],"en":[2091,2107],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_78a.1"},"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 78a:1","assessment":"The Bavli places Rav Rehumi’s report in the preceding passage. Tosafot Yeshanim use it as an objection and offer two possibilities: distinct Ravinas, or an answer Ravina did not himself accept. Rav Rehumi’s observation is not part of Ravina’s direct speech.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 78a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_78a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Yoma 78a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 78a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-021","he":[1332,1395],"en":[2301,2333],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_17a.1"},"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 17a:1","assessment":"The commentary quotes the sequence and asks whether Rav Yosef could have seen Ravina. The primary Bavli gives the words after the Ravina liturgical discussion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 17a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_17a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Ed"},{"reference":"Beitzah 17a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Beitzah_17a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-022","he":[1396,1520],"en":[2405,2601],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_17a.1"},"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 17a:1","assessment":"The exact Shittah gives both alternatives. Preserve the distinction between the voice of Rav Yosef and the possible anonymous narrator.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 17a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_17a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Ed"}]},{"id":"3212:1:link-023","he":[1527,1582],"en":[2618,2699],"target":{"entry":3215,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 3215:1","assessment":"The next joint Ravina dossier after Ravina the Later begins with Avimi and explicitly enumerates figures associated with the earlier and later Ravinas.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3215:1","target":{"entry":3215,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,3,4,5,6,8,10,11,12,13,14,15,17,18,20,21,22],"holds":[{"raw":"אין זה רבינא סתמא שבש\"ס שהיה חבירו של רב אשי","reason":"Semag applies the earlier-Ravina distinction as a conclusion, Tosafot as a possibility, and Rosh as an explanation of the ruling. The title and chronological distinction remain the views of the cited sources.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 48a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_48a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 72b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_72b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rosh on Chullin 3:23:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rosh_on_Chullin_3.23.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"raw":"שהרי רב פפא תלמידו של רבא הוה, ורב כהנא היה תלמיד רבא רבו של רב אשי הוה","reason":"The checked Shittah states these historical premises. The quoted house formula establishes its textual basis for Rav Ashi in Rav Kahana’s school. The full chain remains the commentary’s historical reasoning.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"},{"reference":"Chullin 49a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_49a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ולא יתכן שרב פפא מביא עובדא דרבינא דהוא תלמיד חבר דרב אשי","reason":"This inference appears in a separate voice in the checked Shittah. Heilprin compares the primary text’s Rav Pappi spelling and offers a counterargument. The historical premise stays attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 82a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_82a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ולדרכו איך יביא רב פפי עובדא מתלמיד חבר של תלמידו","reason":"The checked loci give Rav Pappi’s report and Rav Ashi’s study-house formula. The rhetorical analogy is Heilprin’s answer to the commentary’s dating argument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 82a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_82a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 67a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_67a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"כתב בס\"ס נחלה ליהושע","reason":"The direct Shittah comment is located. The exact page in the Nahalah printing remains to collate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Beitzah 17a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Beitzah_17a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Ed"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Semag, Tosafot and Rosh give related arguments with different levels of certainty. The source texts establish what each commentator says.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The checked Shittah reads הר״ף where Heilprin’s text has הריא״ף, and separates the quoted pupil’s passage from another account. The primary mortgage text has Rav Pappi, and Heilprin’s cited Rav Pappi house formula occurs at Hullin 82a.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The two Beitzah explanations distinguish Rav Yosef’s direct speech from a possible anonymous explanation. The underlying Shittah is checked and the specific Nahalah printing remains uncollated.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Shita Mekubetzet on Bava Metzia 67a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shita_Mekubetzet_on_Bava_Metzia_67a.10"},"witness":"Warsaw, 1901"},{"reference":"Tosafot Yeshanim on Yoma 78a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_Yeshanim_on_Yoma_78a.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Yoma 78a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yoma 78a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_78a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
